{title: I Sing the Mighty Power of God}
{artist: Isaac Watts / Ellacombe (1784)}
{genre: Hymn, Children}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: i-sing-the-mighty-power-of-god.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (I_Sing_The_Mighty_Power_Of_God-Ellacombe)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]I [A]sing [G#7]the [E]mighty [F#m]pow'r of [E]God,
[A]That [D]made the [Bm]moun[E]tains [A]rise;
[A]That spread [G#7]the [E]flowing [F#m]seas a[E]broad,
[A]And [D]built [F#m]the [E]lofty [A]skies.
[A]I sing the wis[D]dom [E]that ordained
[A]The sun to rule [D]the [E]day:
[E]The [A]moon [G#7]shines [E]full at [F#m]His com[E]mand,
[A]And [D]all [F#m]the [E]stars o[A]bey.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]I [A]sing [G#7]the [E]goodness [F#m]of the [E]Lord,
[A]That [D]filled the [Bm]earth [E]with [A]food:
[A]Who formed [G#7]the [E]creatures [F#m]with His [E]Word,
[A]And [D]then [F#m]pro[E]nounced them [A]good.
[A]Lord, how Thy won[D]ders [E]are displayed,
[A]Where’er I turn [D]my [E]eye,
[E]If [A]I [G#7]sur[E]vey the [F#m]ground I [E]tread,
[A]Or [D]gaze [F#m]up[E]on the [A]sky!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]There's [A]not [G#7]a [E]plant or [F#m]flow'r be[E]low,
[A]But [D]makes Thy [Bm]glo[E]ries [A]known;
[A]And clouds [G#7]a[E]rise and [F#m]tempests [E]blow,
[A]By [D]or[F#m]der [E]from Thy [A]throne.
[A]Creatures that bor[D]row [E]life from Thee
[A]Are subject to [D]Thy [E]care:
[E]There's [A]not [G#7]a [E]place where [F#m]we can [E]flee,
[A]But [D]God [F#m]is [E]present [A]there.
{end_of_verse}
